<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;Real-time 2x2 MIMO Receiver Implemented on U5303A&apos;s FPGA&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;This example uses SystemVue and U5303A FPGA flow to design and implement a 2x2 MIMO receiver on U5303A&apos;s FPGA based on 802.11ac standard. Going through this example can help you to understand SystemVue and U5303A FPGA flow better, especially how to use SystemVue Hardware Design Library, Xilinx IP cores and handcrafted HDL codes together to create a complicated design, and then simulate and implement the complicated design on U5303A&apos;s open FPGA. In addition, it&apos;s a realistic example of MIMO receiver, you can add your own algorithm implementation based on this example to create your own MIMO receiver.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;1. FPGA Design and Simulation for U5303A&apos;s open FPGA&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;The first step of SystemVue and U5303A FPGA flow is the design and software simulation to test and debug your FPGA design.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;You can review Schematic &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;Design2&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot; for the top level&amp;nbsp;design of FPGA entry and simulation. It uses &lt;STRONG&gt;WLAN_11ac_Source@WLAN 11ac Models&lt;/STRONG&gt; from WLAN 11ac library to generate 2x2 MIMO transmitted signal. The 2x2 MIMO receiver FPGA design is in subnet &lt;STRONG&gt;U5303_FPGA0&lt;/STRONG&gt; of U5303A Design Template. In subnet &lt;STRONG&gt;U5303_FPGA0&lt;/STRONG&gt;, DDC, synchronization and CE &amp;amp; MIMO Demapper are implemented by HDL codes that are generated using Xilinx Vivado HLS. These HDL codes are wrapped up with&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;HDL&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;Model&lt;/STRONG&gt; and integrated into SystemVue graphic design. FFT is implemented using Xilinx CoreGenerator and integrated into SystemVue graphic design using &lt;STRONG&gt;XilinxIPIntegrator Model&lt;/STRONG&gt;. &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;You can run &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;Design2 Analysis&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot; for software simulation to verify this FPGA design. You can observe the demodulated constellation in &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;HDL_Cosim_Constellation&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot;.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;Note: when you run &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;Design2 Analysis&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot;, SystemVue calls ModelSim for HDL co-simulation. ModelSim GUI will be launched to show waveform of CE &amp;amp; MIMO Demapper HDL code simulation. You need input &lt;STRONG&gt;run -all&lt;/STRONG&gt; in ModelSim console to start the HDL simulation. &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;You can also import your own HDL codes to this design and embedded your own algorithm to this real-time MIMO receiver.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;2. FPGA Programming File Automatic Generation for U5303A&apos;s open FPGA&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;After software simulation results is ok, you can open &lt;STRONG&gt;HDL Code Generator1&lt;/STRONG&gt; and just click &lt;STRONG&gt;Generate&lt;/STRONG&gt; to launch a fully automatic flow to generate the final FPGA programming file for U5303A.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;3. Co-simulation between SystemVue and U5303A Hardware to verify the FPGA design &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;After U5303A FPGA programming file is generated, you can do the co-simulation between SystemVue and U5303A hardware to verify your FPGA function. And also, you can use SystemVue to generate 802.11ac 2x2 MIMO signal and download to M8190 AWG in the same design.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;You can review Schematic &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;Design1&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot; for the top level&amp;nbsp;design of co-simulation between SystemVue and U5303A hardware.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp; (1) Hardware connection&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=ltr&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;You should connect M8190&apos;s DIRECT OUT of channel 1and 2 to U5303A&apos;s IN1 and IN2 respectively. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp; (2) Parameter Settings&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=ltr&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;You should open &lt;STRONG&gt;Parameters&lt;/STRONG&gt; tab of &lt;STRONG&gt;Design1&lt;/STRONG&gt; Schematic to specify some parameters for your hardware configuration, such as your M8190 and U5303A addresses and your U5303A&amp;nbsp;FPGA programming file directory.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp; (3) Run procedure&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=ltr&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;i) Download 802.11ac 2x2 MIMO waveform to M8190: &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;Open &lt;STRONG&gt;Design1&lt;/STRONG&gt; Schematic. Drag the slider bar &lt;STRONG&gt;Modulation Mode&lt;/STRONG&gt; to your desired modulation, and drag the slider bar &lt;STRONG&gt;Simulation Mode&lt;/STRONG&gt; to &lt;STRONG&gt;Download Waveform to M8190&lt;/STRONG&gt;. Then run &lt;STRONG&gt;Design1 Analysis&lt;/STRONG&gt;.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;ii) Run the real-time demodulation on U5303A FPGA and display the constellation:&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;Drag the slider bar &lt;STRONG&gt;Simulation Mode&lt;/STRONG&gt; to &lt;STRONG&gt;Real-time Demod with U5303A&lt;/STRONG&gt; and run &lt;STRONG&gt;Design1 Analysis&lt;/STRONG&gt;. Then you can observe the dynamic constellation.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
